# Settings > Updates > System packages (report 047 P3): the Pi 5's capture, the one where `apt-get upgrade` and `apt-get
# dist-upgrade` differ: `upgrade` upgrades 244 packages and keeps 23 back; `dist-upgrade` upgrades those too, adds 34 new
# packages and removes pcmanfm. The page lists the 244 as they are (234 safe, 8 launcher libraries, 16 boot chain: the kernel
# packages apt keeps back and the new kernel packages, raspi-firmware, rpi-eeprom ...) and sends what apt keeps back and the
# removal to "Needs the terminal (18)", with the command (sudo apt-get dist-upgrade) on the page a row opens. PackageKit is
# shown, never changed. A long list: Home / End. Keys only.
# Review only: no golden; the headers are checked against the home grid's.
title updates system packages pi5
review
sizes 640x480 480x800 480x640 720x720 1280x800 480x320
@480x800,480x640 profile pda
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env HARNESS_APPS catalogue
env M5APPSTORE_STATE_DIR /nonexistent/harness-appstore
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30 2026-11-01
wifi 70
bt on
update net on
update build 0.9.1 release arm64
update answer releases-real.json
apt board pi5
apt lists-age 2
home
launch Settings
wait 300
key UP
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
wait 4000
shot updates_pi5_root
expect_text "276 updates"
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 600
shot updates_pi5_list
# the end: "On this board" (PackageKit), above it the removal and what apt keeps back
key END
wait 300
shot updates_pi5_end
expect_text "PackageKit"
key UP
wait 300
key UP
wait 300
shot updates_pi5_terminal_rows
key ENTER
wait 300
shot updates_pi5_command
key ESC
wait 300
shot updates_pi5_back
key ESC
key ESC
wait 300
